    "interpretation": "the aggregate logical error rate is robust to a stale DEM in every scenario tested, even when half the individual predictions change. This does not make stale artifacts harmless: the detector error matrix, the priors and the per-shot predictions all change, and a study that compares decoders on a stale DEM compares them on a model that does not describe its own circuit.  But the failure mode that corrupts the headline number is a stale *primary* artifact (the circuit, or a cache keyed without the noise coordinate), not a stale derived model."
